    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d243">

                <pb facs="0336" n="325" sameAs="frus:frus1937v02/pg325"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.4016/1685a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gilbert</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-10-21T16:00:00-05:00">October 21, 1937—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>111. Your despatch 2994 August 19, 1936, annex 2.<anchor n="14" xml:id="d243-f1"
                    /> Ascertain if practicable and cable confidential information regarding rumored
                    decree that German Jews will not be permitted to leave or return to Germany.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d243-f1" n="14" xml:id="d243-f1-content">
                <p>Annex not printed; for an extract from the despatch, see <ref
                        target="frus1936v02#pg_201"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>,
                        1936, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, p. 201</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
